  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a positive integer NNN, find the nearest multiple of 333.\n\nMultiples of 333 are …−6,−3,0,3,6,9,12,15,…\\ldots -6, -3, 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, \\ldots…−6,−3,0,3,6,9,12,15,….\n\nFormally, find XXX, the multiple of 333 with minimum value of ∣N−X∣|N - X|∣N−X∣.\n\nIt can be proven that the answer is always unique, i.e. 222 different multiples of 333 cannot be nearest at the same time.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line of input contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the nearest multiple of 333.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤101 \\le N \\le 101≤N≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe nearest multiple is 000.\nFor example, 333 is not the answer because ∣1−0∣=1<∣1−3∣=2|1 - 0| = 1 < |1 - 3| = 2∣1−0∣=1<∣1−3∣=2."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe nearest multiple of 333 is 666."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "9",
        "output": "9",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\n999 is itself a multiple of 333."
      }
    ]
  },
